## Pre-work plan

- Background: RFC-PTCS-DYNAMIC-0036 defines a global resident navigator, but released 0.2.8 wires only model helpers and the ResidentCoverageChanged contract. Renderer DOM/gesture/action binding and active client/server wire paths are absent.
- Goal: complete the additive owner path without changing existing inner navigator behavior when GlobalOverview=None.
- Assumptions: Daedalus owns whole-series provider/materialization and 18884 consumer validation; owner packages own generic rendering, action transport, and deterministic tests.
- Steps: add RED owner tests for DOM/order/drop-only/action wire; complete allowlist and active wire cases; add independent global draft/drag settlement and global strip above the inner navigator; run focused and full owner suites; bump packages only after green source commit.
- Scope: Contracts, Renderer, Interactive/Ptcs client transport as required, Server transient compatibility, RFC/WBS/Test/README/DevLog. No Daedalus source or 18884 lifecycle mutation.
- Acceptance: RFC-0036 acceptance 1-7 and 9-10 pass owner tests; global pointermove emits no remote action; one pointerup emits one ResidentCoverageChanged; inner visible width stays unchanged; GlobalOverview=None preserves existing DOM/action behavior.
- Risk: reusing inner draft/action state could clear the wrong gesture. Keep global draft and pending intent independent while sharing the existing single action submission authority.

